    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-045 — inline background-image.** Three commits on one branch, merged only after Commit 2's **scroll-verified** PNG (not first-viewport — all targets are in article body content).\n\n**First cycle this session with scroll-verified (not first-viewport) delta.** Honest framing: 242 external link icons appear next to `WHATWG` / `CERN` / `ISO` etc. starting at char 108015 (~4-5 scroll heights into the article).\n\n## Commits\n\n| # | Scope | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Parse + fragment fields** (behavior-neutral) | ✅ Green — 572 / 2224 tests pass, +10 new |\n| 2 | **Paint** (visible on scroll: external link icons) | ⏳ Pending — scroll-PNG verification before merge |\n| 3 | **Docs** (ADR-045 → Implemented) | ⏳ Pending |\n\n## Measurement (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-29)\n\n**Only 1 renderable rule.** The other 13 of 14 background-size rules target `mask-image` (different subsystem, not implemented).\n\n| Target | Count | Renders |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.mw-parser-output a.external` (background-image + size + position + repeat + padding-right) | 1 | ✅ |\n| mask-image targets | 13 | ❌ deferred |\n\n**242 `.external` elements in article HTML**, first at char 108015.\n\n## Commit 1 details\n\n### The `LayoutText` discovery\n\nInitial diagnostic: `<a>` recurses as its own `LayoutBox`, so its text goes through the **`LayoutText`** path, not `InlineContext`. The post-process is a **shared helper** `apply_inline_bg_pp()` called from both paths — matching existing codebase convention (LayoutText for uniform style, InlineContext for mixed).\n\n### What shipped\n\n- `LineFragment` gains `bg_image_url`, `bg_size_w/h`, `bg_pos_x/y` (enums), `bg_no_repeat`\n- `apply_inline_bg_pp` populates fields from `ComputedStyleMap`\n- Parses `background-image: url(...)`, `background-size` (fixed; cover/contain deferred), `background-position` (keyword pairs, flexible order), `background-repeat` (no-repeat only)\n- **Padding-right** honored: fragment width extended, subsequent same-line fragments shifted → creates icon gap\n\n## Commit 2 preview (visible delta)\n\n- New `paint_inline_image()` helper — mirrors `paint_image` but takes `LineFragment` instead of `LayoutBox`\n- `InlineContext` / `LayoutText` cases in `paint_children` draw backgrounds before glyphs\n- **Position keywords resolve in paint** against loaded icon dimensions (avoids layout-time image loading)\n- **Scroll-PNG verification**: BEFORE / AFTER at first `.external` (~4-5 scroll heights down)\n\n## Why scroll-PNG is legitimate verification here\n\nFirst-viewport PNG is convenient, not the requirement. For a feature whose targets are **article body content** (citations, external links to standards bodies), the natural verification position is where those targets live. Scroll-PNG at the first `.external` link is equivalent rigor: icon either appears (16×14px, unambiguous) or doesn't.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `mask-image` (13 of 14 background-size rules)\n- `background-size: cover | contain`\n- Percentage size / position\n- `background-repeat: repeat | repeat-x | repeat-y`\n- Multi-layer backgrounds\n- `background-clip` / `background-origin`\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-045: 562 cases / 2188 assertions\n- After Commit 1: **572 cases / 2224 assertions** (+10 / +36)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Scroll-PNG verification accepted** — first-viewport delta is zero; targets are article body content. Scroll-PNG at first `.external` (~4-5 scroll heights down) is equivalent rigor.\n- [ ] **Shared helper (LayoutText + InlineContext)** — the `<a>`-goes-through-LayoutText discovery is genuinely how the codebase handles single-element text runs today. Helper extraction covers both. Agree?\n- [ ] **Padding-right extends fragment width** — creates the icon gap. Documented in Commit 1; fragment width += padding, subsequent same-line fragments shifted.\n- [ ] **`mask-image` deferred** — 13 of 14 background-size rules target mask-image (Vector icons, dropdown chevrons, magnify). Different subsystem, own ADR.\n- [ ] **Zero first-viewport delta** — this is the first \"scroll-verified\" cycle. Honest about the tradeoff vs ADR-042/043's first-viewport PNGs.\n\n## DO NOT MERGE until Commit 2's scroll-PNG verification passes.\n\nRefs #218\n",
